    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0228" n="216" xml:id="pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/4293: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-07T13:00:00+00:00">January 7, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Another contingent of about 4000 Italians arrived in Cadiz last week thus making
                    total of approximately 8000 arrivals during the past fortnight exclusive of the
                    Red Cross unit mentioned in my telegram December 30, 1 p.m.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d118-f1"/> These forces are for the most part infantrymen and
                    artillerymen and are said to have come directly from Abyssinia. Cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Baleares</hi> sister ship of Cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Canarias</hi>, recently launched, is now being equipped
                    in Cadiz with guns and will be ready for service within a week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
